<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκομ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carry</i> or <i>bring out,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				294
			</span></i> ; esp. to a place of safety, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.160
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.122
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.6
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκκομίζειν τινὰ ἐκ τοῦ
				μέλλοντος γίνεσθαι πρήγματος</span>
			<i>to keep</i> him <i>out</i> of trouble, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.43
			</span></i> :—
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				8.20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.78
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσεκομίσαντο καὶ ἐξεκομίσαντο
				ἃ ἐβούλοντο,</span> of those relieved from a state of
			siege, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.117
			</span></i> : abs., <i>remove,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τοὺς Λοκρούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.32
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> esp. <i>carry
				out</i> a corpse, <i>bury,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				35.6.2
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cic.</u>
				42
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. σῖτον,</span> of a horse,
			<i>throw</i> the provender <i>out of</i> the manger, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				4.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>carry home,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>An.</u>
					6.6.36
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>endure to the end,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ πεπρωμένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1269
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>receive</i> what is due, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγους, ὀψώνια,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>PLille</u>
				3.79
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.436
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
